<Legal updated="October 2026" title="Pricing" description="How pricing works for Krylabs client projects and its free and paid products, subscriptions and taxes.">

  <p>Krylabs offers a mix of free and paid products. Pricing is shown at the point of purchase and may vary by region and platform. Subscriptions purchased through the App Store are billed by Apple.</p>

  <h2>How pricing works</h2>
  <p>Each product is priced independently. Free apps may offer optional in-app purchases or subscriptions that unlock additional features. Current prices are always displayed in-app or on the product's page before you pay.</p>

  <h2>Client projects</h2>
  <p>iOS app projects for clients are quoted individually after a call about the app. The written
  estimate splits the work into milestones, and each milestone is invoiced when it is delivered, so
  the full amount is never due upfront. <a class="link" href="/#faq">How projects are priced</a>.</p>

  <h2>Payments in India</h2>
  <p>Payments to Krylabs in India are collected in <strong>Indian Rupees (₹ INR)</strong> through
  invoices and payment links issued via RBI-authorised payment aggregators such as Razorpay. The
  exact amount payable, and what it covers, is always stated on the invoice or payment page before
  you pay &mdash; there are no hidden fees. Where a product offers purchases directly on our
  websites or apps (for example, event reservations), the price is displayed the same way before
  you confirm payment.</p>

  <h2>Taxes</h2>
  <p>Prices may be exclusive of applicable taxes, which are calculated and shown at checkout where relevant.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>For pricing questions, email <a href="mailto:info.krylabs@gmail.com">info.krylabs@gmail.com</a>.</p>
</Legal>
